# Line-ending policy (TD-019).
#
# The repository stores text as LF — 225 of 226 tracked text files already did, which this file
# makes explicit rather than incidental. Without it, behaviour depends on each developer's
# `core.autocrlf`, and on Windows that setting rewrites the working tree to CRLF on checkout. That
# is what broke `npm run format:check` after a routine rebase: `.prettierrc` sets
# `endOfLine: "lf"`, so a CRLF working tree fails the format gate while `git status` stays clean —
# 109 files reported as modified that differed only by a carriage return.
#
# `eol=lf` (rather than bare `text=auto`) forces the *working tree* to LF too, so the checked-out
# bytes are the committed bytes on every platform and the Prettier gate means the same thing
# everywhere.
#
# One file was genuinely inconsistent and is normalized alongside this: `schema.sql` was committed
# with CRLF. Verified content-identical afterwards — line endings only.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary, so git never attempts an end-of-line conversion on them. Corrupting an image
# this way is silent: the file still opens in some viewers and fails in others.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
